# Byte-for-byte checkouts, on every platform.
#
# This project's film identity is a CONTENT HASH. `build_id` in the reel's
# coverage.json is the SHA-256 of a map of file paths to the SHA-256 of each
# file's bytes (see scripts/build_source_snapshot.py and the reel's CAPTURE.md),
# and the film's own SHA-256 is recorded beside it. A hash over bytes is only
# reproducible if everyone's checkout has the same bytes.
#
# Without this file it does not. `core.autocrlf` is LOCAL configuration and is
# never distributed with a repository, so a clone on Windows with Git's default
# settings converts every LF to CRLF, changes every text file's length, and
# therefore changes every per-file hash and the build_id derived from them.
#
# That was not hypothetical. An anonymous clone of this repository recomputed
# build_id as e83b9a83... against the 82696a5d... recorded in coverage.json -
# a reviewer following the documented verification would have concluded the
# film did not match the posted source. player.gd alone differed by 354 bytes,
# all of them carriage returns.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion for every path, in both directions,
# so what is committed is exactly what is checked out. That is the property the
# verification needs.
* -text
